<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cockacoeske</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1686</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cockacoeske was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamunkey">Pamunkey</a> leader who ruled as weroansqua from 1656 until her death in 1686. Widow of the chief Totopotomoy, she sought to restore Pamunkey authority over the former Powhatan peoples, and she signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-middle-plantation">Treaty of Middle Plantation</a> in 1677, which made the tribes tributaries of the English Crown while guaranteeing their lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cockacoeske.jpg" alt="Cockacoeske" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kss5pj · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cockacoeske_VWM_Statue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
